;; Struct sequences (PY6e; Objects/structseq.c) for the OS family's results: os.stat_result, os.terminal_size,
;; os.times_result, os.uname_result, os.statvfs_result, os.waitid_result, pwd.struct_passwd, grp.struct_group,
;; resource.struct_rusage. The first nSeq items are a sequence (len, [], iteration, ==, hash as a tuple's); every
;; field is an attribute by name (a name "" is an unnamed field, CPython's NULL member: in the sequence only). Since
;; py-core-1124 a tuple subclass, as CPython's (PyStructSequence's tp_base is tuple): its visible items are its tuple
;; (BaseTuple), so isinstance(r, tuple) holds and tuple's methods see them; the types CPython makes as heap types
;; (PyStructSequence_NewType: the modules' own, not sys's static ones) take attributes (structSeqHeap).

